{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1028530-template-stacking-in-2e","id":1028530,"title":"Template Stacking in 2E","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-08T07:05:43-08:00","id":1028530,"title":"Template Stacking in 2E","content":"First Edition books were clear that you couldn't stack templates, explicitly stating that a Mage dies when embraced, etc, IIRC.<br /> <br /> I actually can't find any mention of any of that, at all, in 2E. I'm sure it's still the assumed state of things, but is this no longer a written rule in 2E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T08:20:15-08:00","id":1028557,"title":"","content":"First, let me say this. &quot;Template&quot; has two meanings. The official definition is actually something along the lines of &quot;group of mechanics that overlay a base mortal.&quot; Meanwhile, there's the unofficial definition that generally means something along the lines of &quot;supernatural race.&quot; You can't really combine the first kind of template - the two are simply incompatable. <br /> <br /> That said? In general, 2e is a lot more crossover friendly than 1e was, and people play in each other's sandboxes a lot more. We have lots of tinkering and not-official stuff that involves mixing supernaturals in the side. We've seen new rule templates made for mixed vamp-'lings. There are legacies and bloodlines and more that mix &quot;races.&quot; <br /> <br /> As far as I can tell, there's no official rule because rules can get in the way of story if you want to do it. There probably won't be an official mixed-breed Sam H. again that runs amok. But that was a different matter entirely from players and STs doing what they want.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T08:50:37-08:00","id":1028567,"title":"","content":"So far in Lore I have not seen any information that would directly prohibit mixed species of the supernatural. Yes, mage lost his Gnosis when Embraced. But not when possessed by Stryx owl. Werewolf also cant be Embraced but can be possessed by Stryx. Can werewolf Awake? It is unlikely - worldview becomes quite unsuitable for <b><u>ruling</u> </b>over the world. But Mage can not forgot what he knew before night of First Change. And what happens in the end? When Mage possessed by Stryx experience First Change? hell knows. Most likely something that exists beyond reality, controlled by God-Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12029-osuneko","name":"OsuNeko","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:12:22-08:00","id":1028612,"title":"","content":"well, considering that Merit Templates (as in Hurt Locker) do not stack, it looks like the general case is that Template stacking is not the consensus even in 2E. There are exceptions (like having a Strix using Synthesis, and certain minor templates &quot;evolving&quot; to the corresponding major templates, like Proximi into Mages and I think Wold Blooded into Werewolves), or things like the Admonitoria (which is not canon)- but there is no sign they are going to allow Werewolves to Awaken or something like that. If there is a change, I guess we would see it in the Crossover Chronicles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:26:27-08:00","id":1028616,"title":"","content":"The edges of the maps blur, but the edge is not the whole of the map.<br /> <br /> By and large, major templates don't stack-the most they do is fuse, ala non-canon Admonitoria. However, introduce lesser templates or weird ass powers, and the entire thing becomes murkier. It's not just Strix/Idigam edge cases either-the Matrimony Oath in Secrets of the Covenants puts some weird fuckery in there, a Demon-Blooded might carry their Embeds and Ciphers into awakening, as might a Wolf-Blooded, and weirder cases around.<br /> <br /> Rarity and Weirdness, with an emphasis on warping, tends to constitute my thoughts on the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:29:46-08:00","id":1028619,"title":"","content":"But as hard rules goes, the writing still assumes major templates don't stack, should not miss that.<br /> <br /> Course, at your own table, that can go out the window, and we do like edge cases. I know I've got an itch to see what happens when a demon defies a Stranger and <i>loses</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T11:40:23-08:00","id":1028621,"title":"","content":"People who were Wolf-Blooded maintain their Tell as they change into a major template. But your Storyteller can deem otherwise.<br /> <br /> Also technically since Pure and Forsaken are two different templates, you can switch from one major template to another there.<br /> <br /> But mostly the 'ruling' is that your minor template abilities disappear when you join a major one, and a major one can't usually change beyond weird circumstances, like changing to Pure, or a Promethean changing to human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}